{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Anti-MRSA, Antibiofilm", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Discovery: S9 splits the hydrophobic surface of LL-37. SK-24 corresponds to the central helix starting S9. Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals this sequence is most similar (88.89%) to Human KS-27 K: 21%; R: 13%; I: 13%. GRAVY: -0.69; Activity: Active against E. faecium V284-17 (MIC 2 uM), S. aureus USA300 (MIC 4 uM), K-pneumoniae E406-17 (MIC>32 uM). A. baumannii B28-16 (MIC 4-8 uM), P-aeruginosa E411-17 (MIC > 32 uM), and E. coli E423-17 (MIC 16 uM). It also dispersed preformed biofilms of both A. baumannii and S. aureus USA300. Structure: Like LL-37, SK-24 is helical even in PBS, more helical than that after binding to SDS. MOA:bacteria: it permeated bacterial membranes. In vitro Toxicity: it was least hemo.lytic (HC50 > 200 uM) compared to LL-37 and its fragments, including 17BIPHE2 at 200 uM. Updated 6/2025", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "34959645", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Pharmaceuticals (Basel). 2021 Nov 30;14(12):1245. doi: 10.3390/ph14121245. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03768", "source_id": "AP03768", "source_numeric_id": "03768", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03768", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Structure and Activity of a Selective Antibiofilm Peptide SK-24 Derived from the NMR Structure of Human Cathelicidin LL-37.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
